Palangkaraya crew: C4, then C11, then C2. Jambi City crew: C5, then C1. Banjarbaru crew: C73, then C3. Visiting is not extinguishing.

Water: C11 river 3820 m SW, C2 river 5700 m NE, C5 river 5110 m SE. No river was seen near C4, C1, C73 and C3 within the searched distance; canals are not detected.", "caveats": ["Earliest detection is the first satellite detection, not the ignition point, and 4 of the top 5 clusters were already burning at the start of the 2019-09-09 to 2019-09-15 window with 5449 detections today.", "There are 105 P1 brigade now clusters, 361 P2 village fire watch clusters and 5488 P3 monitor clusters from peat weighted forecast risk.", "Crew routes assume 1 crew per provincial capital at 30.0 km per hour with route factor 1.4 and 2.0 hours on site within a 10.0 hour day, maximising peat weighted risk covered; visiting a fire is not extinguishing it.", "River search used Sentinel-2 imagery with SAM 3.1 masks for rivers only on a 10 x 10 km chip centred on the cluster within 5.1 km each side; drainage canals are too narrow at 10 m pixels and are not detected, so no river seen does not mean no water at all.", "Spread forecast for 2019-09-16 expects 2266.5 new 1.1 km cells across 130413 candidate cells; new fire watch scored 9013 quiet 11 km cells with 810 cells above threshold."] }
